### Matt Olson Bio
#### 2023
exit velo (fourth, 93.7), OPS(fourth, .993), hard-hit balls (fifth, 247), fWAR (fifth, 6.7)...29-year-old Matt Olson completed his eighth Major League season (second with Atlanta), posting a slash line of .283/389/.604 (172-for- 608) in 162 games...He hit 54 home runs, 27 doubles and three triples, while recording 139 RBI and 127 runs...Established career-highs in runs, hits, home runs, triples, RBI, walks (104), on-base percentage and total bases (367)...Established the Braves single-season records for home runs (54) and RBI (139) - since RBI became official in 1920...Joined Hall-of-Famer Henry Aaron (1957, '60, '63, '66) as the only players in franchise history to lead the Majors in RBI...Aaron, like Olson, led the Majors in both categories in 1957...Of his 54 home runs, 28 were hit at Truist Park; most by any player at their home venue...The only player in franchise history with more home runs at their home venue, within a single season, is Hall-of-Famer Henry Aaron (31) at Atlanta Stadium in 1971...Made his sixth career Opening Day roster (second with Atlanta)...Has started at first base in his club's season opener in each of the last six seasons: 2018-21 with Oakland and '22-23 with Atlanta...Started all 162 of Atlanta's games during the regular season; all at first base...He's played in all 162 regular season games in each of his first two seasons with the Braves...Dating to May 2, 2021, he's played in 458 consecutive regular season games;
